{
  "_about": "The closed vocabulary of what can happen, with the balanced entry each one makes. A leg names an account (literal, or a template in braces) or a category, and an amount expression over the event's fields. Sign: positive is a debit (asset or expense goes up), negative is a credit (liability or income goes up). The engine evaluates these templates; no event kind posts in code. Legs with a zero amount are dropped. Every kind MUST sum to zero for any field values, which tools/generate.js proves symbolically. Holdings are carried at market: a sale moves proceeds out of the holding, the next price moves the rest through revaluation, and tax gains live in lot_match, so net worth never jumps at a sale.",
